{"name":"Japanese Horseradish","hex":"#a8bf93","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"horseradish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the mustard family, Armoracia rusticana, cultivated for its edible root.","A pungent condiment made from the root of the plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horseradish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wasabi","blocks":[{"text":"Wasabi or Japanese horseradish is a plant of the family Brassicaceae, which also includes horseradish and mustard in other genera. The plant is native to Japan, the Russian Far East including Sakhalin, and the Korean Peninsula. It grows naturally along stream beds in mountain river valleys in Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Wasabia_japonica_4.JPG/330px-Wasabia_japonica_4.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wasabi","wikidata":"Q49855"},{"title":"Horseradish","blocks":[{"text":"Horseradish is a perennial plant of the family Brassicaceae. It is a root vegetable, cultivated and used worldwide as a spice and as a condiment. The species is likely native to Southeastern Europe and Western Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Armoracia_rusticana.jpg/330px-Armoracia_rusticana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horseradish","wikidata":"Q26545"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Fresh_wasabi_rhizomes.jpg/500px-Fresh_wasabi_rhizomes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Fresh_wasabi_rhizomes.jpg/500px-Fresh_wasabi_rhizomes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresh wasabi stems","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFresh_wasabi_rhizomes.jpg"},{"